+### opencode-241
+
+Where a caller supplies `outputSchema`, when the native prompt dispatches, the adapter shall request a native JSON-schema envelope containing `result`, correlate the completed assistant submission to the current prompt's message and root session, and expose that exact object as terminal result text without accepting a foreign, incomplete or failed assistant submission.
+
 ## Verification
 
 ### opencode-62
@@ -1170,6 +1174,10 @@ Where the installed OpenCode CLI is on the path, when a managed run selecting `n
 
 Where [[opencode-219](#opencode-219)]'s credential, retry, and skip preconditions hold in managed mode, when a run supplies a fixture skill whose body directs a unique token reply and the prompt names the skill, the acceptance check shall verify against the real server that its skill list carries the skill at the carrier location [[opencode-69](#opencode-69)], that the reply carries the token [[opencode-67](#opencode-67)], and that the carrier root is gone once the adapter's own event stream completes [[opencode-71](#opencode-71)].
 
+### opencode-242
+
+When an installed-SDK integration and a live structured-output run exercise native and foreign assistant submissions, they shall verify prompt schema delivery, current-message correlation and exact terminal JSON [[opencode-241](#opencode-241)].
+
